<div class="hero"><span class="flag">🇧🇩</span><h1>From Bangladesh to China: Advanced Care, Accessible Prices</h1><p>For complex cardiac surgery, advanced cancer treatment, organ transplant and IVF, China's JCI-accredited and Grade 3A hospitals offer treatments that are often unavailable or limited in Bangladesh — at a fraction of US, UK and Singapore prices.</p><a href="/contact-new.html?source=bangladesh-landing" class="btn-red">Start Free Case Review &rarr;</a></div>

<div class="card"><h2>Cost Comparison: China vs US / UK / Singapore (2026)</h2>
<table><tr><th>Procedure</th><th>China</th><th>US / UK / SG</th></tr>
<tr><td>Heart Bypass (CABG)</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$12K-$18K</td><td>$100K-$150K (US)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Heart Valve Replacement</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$10K-$15K</td><td>$80K-$120K (US)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cancer Treatment</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$8K-$20K</td><td>$50K-$100K (US)</td></tr>
<tr><td>IVF (1 cycle)</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$3K-$8K</td><td>$15K-$25K (US)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Spine Surgery</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$10K-$18K</td><td>$40K-$80K (US)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Knee Replacement</td><td style="color:#2e7d32;font-weight:700">$8K-$12K</td><td>$35K-$50K (US)</td></tr></table>
<p style="font-size:.85rem;color:#888">Prices are 2026 estimates for total in-hospital cost. Bangladesh patients usually travel for <strong>advanced or complex care</strong> — the price comparison is against Western/Singapore private care, not routine care in Bangladesh. Transplant and CAR-T are priced per case. Final cost depends on hospital and clinical complexity.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h2>Why Bangladeshi Patients Choose China for Treatment</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Treatments not always available at home:</strong> complex cardiac surgery, CAR-T and immunotherapy for cancer, organ transplant, and advanced neurosurgery are core strengths of China's top hospitals.</li><li><strong>Direct flights:</strong> Dhaka to Kunming (about 3 hours), Dhaka to Guangzhou (about 4 hours), and connections onward to Beijing and Shanghai.</li><li><strong>English-speaking doctors:</strong> All recommended hospitals have international departments with fluent English staff.</li><li><strong>JCI accreditation:</strong> Top Chinese hospitals meet the same standards as leading US academic centers.</li><li><strong>L visa:</strong> Bangladeshi citizens need an L (tourist/medical) or S2 visa, applied for at the Chinese Embassy in Dhaka; hospitals provide invitation letters to support the application. See the <a href="/visa-guide.html" style="color:#1e3c72;font-weight:600">visa guide</a> for every option.</li><li><strong>Start small with imaging:</strong> Not ready for surgery? Book an <a href="/medical-imaging.html" style="color:#1e3c72;font-weight:600">MRI or CT scan</a> from $150 — scheduled within 24–48 hours.</li></ul></div>

<div class="card"><h2>How We Help Bangladeshi Patients</h2><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Tell us your condition, records, and timing — free, no commitment.</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We match you with 2-3 hospitals and compare costs, with transport and visa guidance.</p><p><strong>Step 3:</strong> We coordinate records, appointments, invitation letters, and airport pickup. You fly from Dhaka — we handle the rest.</p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> From $49 (hospital shortlist) to $399 (full journey management), with $149 verification in between. No hidden fees, no hospital commissions. <a href="pricing.html">See pricing →</a></p></div>

